      "content": "\"Makan hati\" translates to \"let's get down to dessert\" in English, suggesting that it's time to relax. In the Indonesian context, it's a playful and friendly phrase used to encourage open conversations, often about delicious food or ending a formal event positively. Using it could be a great way to end your opening remarks and signal your excitement for an informal chat with the delegates. Just be sure your delivery matches the friendly context. Everyone will love your attention to detail and eagerness to connect.",
